-- title:
--   Fricke stability of a toric lattice in Tₚ J_H(M), up to p-powers
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $p \mid M$ (with $M$ and $M/p$ nonzero), a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and write $J_H(M)$ for the degree-zero divisor class group `Pic0` of the function field $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$ (the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of Laurent series generated by the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational one), and $J_{H'}(M/p)$ likewise for $H' = \mathrm{infSubgroup}$, the image of $H$ under $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$; here $T = \mathrm{TateModule}\,p\,J_H(M)$ consists of the sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_H(M)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$, a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module, and $T'$ is its analogue at level $M/p$. Given a valuation subring $Pl$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit in it, a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-submodule $T^{\mathrm{t}} \subseteq T$, $\mathbb{Z}_p$-linear maps $\mathrm{push}_0,\mathrm{push}_1 : T \to T'$ and $\mathrm{pull}_0,\mathrm{pull}_1 : T' \to T$, and $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphisms $w$, $w'$ of the two function fields, acting on divisor classes through the associated semilinear automorphisms and on Tate modules through `JH.tateEnd`, assume: the action of $w$ on $J_H(M)$ is an involution and commutes with the action of every element of the inertia subgroup $I$ of $Pl$ inside $\mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$; the action of $w'$ on $J_{H'}(M/p)$ is an involution; every $\tau \in I$ acts on $T^{\mathrm{t}}$ by the scalar given by the $p$-adic cyclotomic character $\chi(\tau)$; $\mathrm{push}_0$ and $\mathrm{push}_1$ vanish on $T^{\mathrm{t}}$; for some $k$, $p^k(\tau - 1)T \subseteq T^{\mathrm{t}} + \mathrm{im}\,\mathrm{pull}_0 + \mathrm{im}\,\mathrm{pull}_1$ for all $\tau \in I$; the only element of $\mathrm{im}\,\mathrm{pull}_0 + \mathrm{im}\,\mathrm{pull}_1$ killed by both $\mathrm{push}_0$ and $\mathrm{push}_1$ is $0$; $\mathrm{push}_1 \circ w = w' \circ \mathrm{push}_0$ on $T$; and some $\tau_0 \in I$ has $\chi(\tau_0) = 1 + p$. Then there is $k' \in \mathbb{N}$ with $p^{k'} w(x) \in T^{\mathrm{t}}$ for every $x \in T^{\mathrm{t}}$.
--
--   This is the stability, up to bounded $p$-power denominators, of a toric lattice in the $p$-adic Tate module of $J_H(M)$ under the Fricke involution in the case $p \,\|\, M$, formulated entirely in terms of hypotheses on the inertia action, the two degeneracy push-forwards and pull-backs, and the interchange law relating $w$ at level $M$ with $w'$ at level $M/p$. It feeds the level-lowering step that identifies the Fricke-twisted behaviour of the toric part, being cited by the statement about $p$-power multiples of Weil-pairing-trivial Fricke classes in the diamond-fixed Tate module at level divisible by $p$ but not $p^2$.
